{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And I will meet you there.</b> He returns to the altar that he mentioned — this is the altar of burnt offering. From here the Rabbis of blessed memory learned that the Holy One, blessed be He, would speak with Moses from atop the altar of bronze once the Tabernacle was erected." "<b>And there are</b> some among the Sages who would say that He spoke from atop the cover (kapporet), as it is said (Exodus 25:22): ״ודברתי אתך מעל הכפרת״. And what he mentioned — ״where I will appoint a meeting with you, to speak to you there״ — the intent is not upon the altar, but upon the Tent of Meeting, which he mentioned: ״at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting before YHWH.״" "<b>And it shall be sanctified by My glory.</b> — that the Shekhinah would rest upon it. And in the Midrash: ״ונקדש בכבודי״ — do not read בכבודי but במכובדין שלי (with My honored ones); this alludes to him the death of the sons of Aaron. And from here Moses said (Leviticus 10:3): ״זה הדבר אשר דבר ה׳ לאמר בקרובי אקדש״. And where did He speak ״בקרובי אקדש״? When He said: ״ונקדש בכבודי״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:29.301380224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}